# Caddy reverse proxy for Sarf.
#
# THIS IS AN EXAMPLE, and only Sarf's own two site blocks. The machine this was
# taken from fronts several unrelated projects from one Caddyfile; publishing
# that file verbatim would publish a map of every other service on the box —
# its hostnames, its loopback ports and where its files live. None of that is a
# credential and all of it is reconnaissance, so it does not belong in a public
# repository. Copy these blocks into your own Caddyfile rather than replacing
# it with this one.
#
# Both hosts front the same FastAPI process on 127.0.0.1:8760 — the split is a
# path allowlist per audience, not two deployments.

# Frontend: dashboard, in-chat signer, and the REST API they call (same-origin,
# so no CORS surface). This is what SARF_PUBLIC_URL points at — every
# proposal's sign_url is minted on this host.
sarf.example.com {
	encode zstd gzip

	# EVERY client-side route must be listed. A page missing from here 404s
	# at the proxy and never reaches the app, which looks like a broken
	# build rather than a config gap — /deposit shipped that way.
	@allowed path / /assets/* /portfolio /markets /how /security /connect /settings /activity /deposit /send /sign /approve /authorize /favicon.ico /dashboard /dashboard/* /legacy /legacy/* /api/* /.well-known/* /healthz
	handle @allowed {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8760
	}
	handle {
		respond 404
	}
}

# MCP endpoint for Claude / ChatGPT connectors. Nothing but the MCP transport
# (and health) is reachable on this host.
#
# The separation is deliberate: the connector host cannot reach /api/*, so a
# connector URL handed to a third party is not also a handle on the session API.
sarf-mcp.example.com {
	encode zstd gzip

	@allowed path /mcp /mcp/* /.well-known/* /healthz
	handle @allowed {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8760
	}
	handle {
		respond 404
	}
}

# The tx-builder sidecar (was 127.0.0.1:8761) must never appear in a site block.
# It is retired in the X Layer build and there is nothing to proxy, but the rule
# stands for anything else added later that binds to loopback: loopback-only is
# the security property, and a reverse_proxy line is what removes it.
